<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Mazorca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1830s–<a href="/years/1852">1852</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Mazorca was the armed wing of the Sociedad Popular Restauradora, a club of supporters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-manuel-de-rosas">Juan Manuel de Rosas</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>. Its members terrorised Unitarian opponents with threats, beatings and murders, with waves of killings in 1840 and 1842. It disappeared after Rosas's fall in 1852.</p></div>
